WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.186
Week 25: Future, Probability, and Forecasting. make forecasts state commitments express probability about the present

2
00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:16.543
Form and meaning. Simple future; irregular stems; future of probability; time clauses referring to future events.

3
00:00:16.543 --> 00:00:44.081
Model set. La población urbana aumentará. Seguiremos midiendo los resultados. ¿Dónde estará Marta ahora? Cuando termine el estudio, publicaremos los datos. Dentro de cinco años habrá nuevas opciones. The urban population will increase. We will continue measuring the results. Where could Marta be now? When the study ends, we will publish the data. In five years there will be new options.

4
00:00:44.081 --> 00:00:54.296
Contrastive practice. Change the person, time, number, or level of formality in each model. Preserve the communicative purpose while the grammar changes.

5
00:00:54.296 --> 00:01:06.581
Production check. Say one original sentence for each function: make forecasts; state commitments; express probability about the present. Then write it and compare the spoken and written forms.

6
00:01:06.581 --> 00:01:35.079
Model language. La población urbana aumentará. — The urban population will increase. Seguiremos midiendo los resultados. — We will continue measuring the results. ¿Dónde estará Marta ahora? — Where could Marta be now? Cuando termine el estudio, publicaremos los datos. — When the study ends, we will publish the data. Dentro de cinco años habrá nuevas opciones. — In five years there will be new options.

7
00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:44.998
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
